        rdfs:comment                   "The complete piece would have been intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en , "Textile, silk wrapped garment, Sindh, ca. 1855-1879."@en , "Wrapped garment, silk woven with pink, yellow, red and black stripes, with a geometric design and a black and white stripe; a deep end border of pink floss silk, with coloured bands in a geometric design at either side. The reverse of the end border is green, and intended to be reversible."@en ;
